Job Description
About Royal HaskoningDHV South Africa
Royal HaskoningDHV South Africa is a consulting engineering company that provides services in various sectors, such as aviation, buildings, energy, industry, infrastructure, maritime, urban development, and water. The company has a long history of innovation and excellence, dating back to 1922 when it was founded as SSI Engineers and Environmental Consultants in Johannesburg. The company is part of the global Royal HaskoningDHV group, which leverages cutting-edge technology and software to enhance society together.
Why should you consider Royal HaskoningDHV South Africa?
Royal HaskoningDHV South Africa offers flexible working hours and allows working from home. This can help you balance your work and personal life, reduce commuting costs and stress, and increase your productivity and satisfaction.
You will be part of a worldwide engineering, project management and consultancy firm with 140 years of experience and 6000 colleagues in 140 countries.
You will work on projects that positively impact people, the environment, and the economy in Southern Africa and beyond.
You will have opportunities to develop yourself in various fields, such as engineering, consultancy, project management, asset management, data science, IT, business development and sales.
You will be supported by cutting-edge technology and software to enhance society together.
You will enjoy a working environment where you feel at home and cared for, where you can help, educate, and inspire each other, and where you can flourish as a professional.
About the Role
We have an exciting opportunity for Junior Architects to join our thriving Architecture teams in the Mission Critical Facilities and Industry Advisory Groups in our Johannesburg / Cape Town / Umhlanga offices of Royal HaskoningDHV.
Job Requirements
Desired Qualifications and Professional Registration
Bachelor of Architecture Degree (Master of Architecture Degree preferred);
Registered / eligible to register as a Candidate Professional Architect with SACAP (not Technologist / Draughting person, etc);
Minimum of 0 – 3+ years relevant experience, preferably within the consulting engineering built environment;
High level of computer literacy (MS Office including advanced Excel skills);
BIM and Revit proficiency (advanced level);
Navisworks, Enscape and Revizto plus Photo-shop capability is an advantage
Knowledge of Dynamo, Python, and other ways to automate your work are highly beneficial;
Experience / knowledge of Revizto, Autodesk Construction Cloud, Common Data Environments and other relevant platforms are highly beneficial;
Autodesk AutoCAD (for legacy projects mainly since primary software is Revit)
Duties and Responsibilities
We will entrust and rely on you to:
Prepare/assist with Inception reports, concept schematic drawings and architectural packages to support Senior Design Architect;
Efficiently engineer and model design using technical and 3D/BIM modeling skills;
Prepare/assist with reports, technical drawings and architectural specifications and tender documentation;
Measuring and compiling of as built information;
Perform/assist in site inspections and attending meetings;
Perform research and investigations;
Provide technical and administrative support with preparation of bid submissions;
Assist with components of architectural tasks inherent to the building’s projects on Revit;
Ensure that all quality system procedures are followed in the production and issuing of designs, costing, drawings and standard details;
Regular contact and communication with the Senior Design Architect;
Perform any other work tasks duly assigned by the Senior Design Architect.
